From 7315a4d6d2305adf197712658839e45df92dbba0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mabn <github@mabn.pl>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:52:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 154/156] [barreplay] H126: the LOS update's map work as one
 set of tasks across types and ally teams (toggle3 0x400000)

speed62's late window: P7's finish ran one task per sensor type, so the main
thread spent 2.4% running types itself and 1.0% waiting for the heaviest one
(ILosType::Update is mostly the map's add and remove loops, LosMap.cpp:464).
ILosType::Update is now BrUpdateBegin (its queues and filtering) + the map
work + BrUpdateEnd (the cache), and with H126 every type's map work runs as
one set of tasks: per type, the unit loop and BrUpdateBegin, then every
type's raycasts at once, then each (type, ally team)'s removes and adds, then
per type the cache. A recalculated instance's old squares are moved aside
before its raycast, so the raycast can run first and its removal still
subtracts what was added. A type's own state is touched only in its first and
last step; a map step writes one ally team's map with integer adds, which
commute. Only in full view, where a visible add's report of squares entering
LOS (CReadMap::UpdateLOS) returns at once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
